null genotype in relation to gender, age and smoking status in Japanese lung cancer patients. Pharmacogenetics. 1995;5:S74–S79. doi: 10.1097/00008571-199512001-00005. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 48. Alexandrie AK, Sundberg MI, Seidegard J, et al. Genetic susceptibility to lung cancer with special emphasis on CYP1A1 and GSTM1: a study on host factors in relation to age at onset, gender and histological cancer types. Carcinogenesis. 1994;15:1785–1790. doi: 10.1093/carcin/15.9.1785. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 49. Dresler CM, Fratelli C, Babb J, et al. Gender differences in genetic susceptibility for lung cancer. Lung Cancer. 2000;30:153–160. doi: 10.1016/s0169-5002(00)00163-x. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 50. Thomsen JS, Wang X, Hines RN, et al. Restoration of aryl hydrocarbon (Ah) responsiveness in MDA-MB-231 human breast cancer cells by transient expression of the estrogen receptor. Carcinogenesis. 1994;15:933–937. doi: 10.1093/carcin/15.5.933. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 51. Mollerup S, Berge G, Baera R, et al. Sex differences in risk of lung cancer: expression of genes in the PAH bioactivation pathway in relation to smoking and bulky DNA adducts. Int J Cancer. 2006;119:741–744. doi: 10.1002/ijc.21891. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 52. Kreuzer M, Gerken M, Heinrich J, et al. Hormonal factors and risk of lung cancer among women? Int J Epidemiol. 2003;32:263–271. doi: 10.1093/ije/dyg064. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 53. Schabath MB, Wu X, Vassilopoulou-Sellin R, et al. Hormone replacement therapy and lung cancer risk: a case-control analysis. Clin Cancer Res. 2004;10:113–123. doi: 10.1158/1078-0432.ccr-0911-3. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 54. Taioli E, Wynder EL. Re: Endocrine factors and adenocarcinoma of the lung in women. J Natl Cancer Inst. 1994;86:869–870. doi: 10.1093/jnci/86.11.869. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 55. Liu Y, Inoue M, Sobue T, et al. Reproductive factors, hormone use and the