Romanis EC. Translational or translationable? A call for ethno-immersion in (empirical) bioethics research. Bioethics. 2024;38(3):252–61. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 22. Lanphier E, Churchill LR. Editors’ introduction to the special issue on the translational work of bioethics. Perspect Biol Med. 2022;65(4):515–20. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 23. Wilson J, Hume J, O’Donovan C, Smallman M. Providing ethics advice in a pandemic, in theory and in practice: A taxonomy of ethics advice. Bioethics. 2024;38(3):213–22. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 24. Cribb A. Translational ethics? The theory-practice gap in medical ethics. J Med Ethics. 2010;36(4):207–10. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 25. Sisk BA, Mozersky J, Antes AL, DuBois JM. The Ought-Is problem: an implementation science framework for translating ethical norms into practice. Am J Bioeth. 2020;20(4):62–70. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 26. Rothstein MA. Translational bioethics and health privacy. Ethics Hum Res. 2023;45(3):40–4. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 27. Evans JH. Translational bioethical Decision-Making: human brain organoids as a case study. Ethics Hum Res. 2024;46(4):47–51. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 28. Mertz M, Fischer T, Salloch S. The value of bioethical research: A qualitative literature analysis of researchers’ statements. PLoS ONE. 2019;14(7). [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] 29. Bærøe K, Henden E. Translational Ethics and Challenges Involved in Putting Norms Into Practice. Vol. 20, American Journal of Bioethics. Routledge. 2020;71–3. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] 30. Majumder MA, Fasipe T. Translational research and health equity: gene therapies for sickle cell disease as a case study. Ethics Hum Res. 2024;46(3). [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] 31. Rothstein MA. Expanding the role of bioethics in translational science. J Law Med Ethics. 2022;50(3):603–7. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 32. Alanazi ENS, Alanazi GJB, Almermesh A