TJ, Aubouy A, Balloux F, Besnard P, Bogreau H, Carnevale P, D''Alessandro U, Fontenille D, Gamboa D, Jombart T, Le Mire J, Leroy E, Maestre A, Mayxay M, Ménard D, Musset L, Newton PN, Nkoghé D, Noya O, Ollomo B, Rogier C, Veron V, Wide A, Zakeri S, Carme B, Legrand E, Chevillon C, Ayala FJ, Renaud F, Prugnolle F. Multiple independent introductions of Plasmodium falciparum in South America. Proc Natl Acad Sci USA. 2012;109:511–516. doi: 10.1073/pnas.1119058109. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 55. Gunawardena S, Ferreira MU, Kapilananda GM, Wirth DF, Karunaweera ND. The Sri Lankan paradox: high genetic diversity in Plasmodium vivax populations despite decreasing levels of malaria transmission. Parasitology. 2014;141:880–890. doi: 10.1017/S0031182013002278. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 56. Koepfli C, Timinao L, Antao T, Barry AE, Siba P, Mueller I, Felger I. A large Plasmodium vivax reservoir and little population structure in the South Pacific. PLoS One. 2013;18:e66041. doi: 10.1371/journal.pone.0066041. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 57. Iwagami M, Hwang SY, Kim SH, Park SJ, Lee GY, Matsumoto-Takahashi EL, Kho WG, Kano S. Microsatellite DNA analysis revealed a drastic genetic change of Plasmodium vivax population in the Republic of Korea during 2002 and 2003. PLoS Negl Trop Dis. 2013;7:e2522. doi: 10.1371/journal.pntd.0002522. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 58. Gravel S, Henn BM, Gutenkunst RN, Indap AR, Marth GT, Clark AG, Yu F, Gibbs RA, 1000 Genomes Project, Bustamante CD Demographic history and rare allele sharing among human populations. Proc Natl Acad Sci USA. 2011;108:11983–11988. doi: 10.1073/pnas.1019276108. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 59. Lachance J, Tishkoff SA. SNP ascertainment bias in population genetic analyses: why it is important, and how to correct it. BioEssays. 2013;35:780–786. doi: 10.1002/bies.201300014.